BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Job Search Tools
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T153000
UID:6a1863f2f6bd012f006af00a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class provides a brief overview of techniques and tools t
 o support job hunters.\nIn this class you will:\n- Consider how to get you
 r job search organized\n- Find & explore job postings\n- Explore governmen
 t sites and services\n- Learn about TPL resources: Career Cruising\, Linke
 dIn Learning\, and Scott’s Business Directories\nPrerequisites: Mouse 
 and keyboarding skills required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1863f2f6bd012f006af00a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee & Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T143000
UID:69c7d087b48451fc3c0bc92a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and informal discussion about 
 services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and le
 t us know what information and resources you would like to access at the l
 ibrary and in the community.\nEach month we will be joined by a different 
 community organization.\nDrop in for some coffee\, snacks\, and a chat wit
 h library staff\, meet other library users\, and learn about local commun
 ity organizations.\nUpcoming guest organizations:\nApril 15: New Circles\n
 May 20: AWHL Senior Safety line and Ve'ahavta\nJune 17: Mosaic Home Care
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, eLearning Lab\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c7d087b48451fc3c0bc92a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Graphic Novel Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T193000
UID:69f8ee7fe8af4a2f00702490@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every month to discuss a variety of graphic novels\, c
 omics\, and manga!\nFor June we will be reading and discussing\nHereditary
  Triangle\nby Fumiya Hayashi.\nPrint copies are available for hold at TPL.
 ca.\nHereditary Triangle\nThis program is hosted by the Arts Department
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founders Room on the first Floor of t
 he Library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f8ee7fe8af4a2f00702490
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monday Night at the Movies!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T200000
UID:6a1622b02ea730c17ab1e91f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy a night at the Port Union Cinema!\nWe will be showi
 ng the following movie at this event:\nElio\nElio\, a space fanatic with a
 n active imagination\, finds himself on a cosmic misadventure where he mus
 t form new bonds with alien lifeforms\, navigate a crisis of intergalactic
  proportions and somehow discover who he is truly meant to be.\nThis is a 
 BYoP event. (Bring Your Own Popcorn.)**
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1622b02ea730c17ab1e91f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monday Night at the Movies!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260615T200000
UID:6a16220e2ea730c17ab1e907@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come enjoy a night at the Port Union Cinema!\nWe will be showi
 ng the following movie at this event:\nThunderBolts\nAfter finding themsel
 ves ensnared in a death trap set by Valentina Allegra de Fontaine\, these 
 disillusioned castoffs must embark on a dangerous mission that will force 
 them to confront the darkest corners of their pasts. Will this dysfunction
 al group tear themselves apart\, or find redemption and unite as something
  much more before it's too late?\nThis is a BYoP event. (Bring Your Own Po
 pcorn.)**
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a16220e2ea730c17ab1e907
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
