BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Memoirs of Pause by Nanhee Kim
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T235959
UID:69e8e6edb6c4ac1fedce0186@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of May\, the works of artist Nanhee Kim a
 re on display at Deer Park branch in an exhibit titled Memoirs of Pause.\
 nNanhee Kim is a multi-disciplinary artist\, fashion/textile designer and 
 educator based in Toronto. Her work has been exhibited at Cambridge Art 
 Galleries/Idea Exchange and the Rochester Memorial Art Gallery (USA). Kim
 ’s awards include research and creation grants in visual arts from Canad
 a Council for the Arts. Her professional experience includes working as 
 an assistant professor at Toronto Metropolitan University’s School of Fa
 shion and as a fashion designer in New York City and Vancouver.\n"My work 
 is inspired by the ephemeral tranquility\, escapism and inner peace that n
 ature provides to people. I seek to observe and emulate nature’s funda
 mental design in my artistic practice\, producing unexpected dimensions an
 d continuous motion in my work. I reimagine visual narratives to depict t
 he feelings and emotions that people experience when interacting with natu
 re. The resulting creations invite observers to encounter meditative pavi
 lions."\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Publ
 ic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locat
 ions across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural i
 nterests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed du
 ring Deer Park branch open hours. Please check the\nDeer Park\nbranch pag
 e before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Nanhee
  Kim\; Title of Piece: Pause No. 2\; Medium: Ink with mulberry paper on ca
 nvas\; Size/Dimensions: Medium
LOCATION:Deer Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8e6edb6c4ac1fedce0186
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
