BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashion for the Planet: Conscious Consumption
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T200000
UID:6a049e6bc6a1dc3d00d379c0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:With the rise of fast fashion brands and social media fueled c
 onsumption habits\, the fashion industry ranks as the 3rd most environment
 ally damaging industry. Everyone participates in this in some way\, so it 
 is important that people are given the information and tools to consume cl
 othing responsibly. This 4 session program will work towards providing sus
 tainable fashion literacy to participants by teaching them the environment
 al impacts of the fashion industry\, tips for conscious consumption\, and 
 practical tools to extend the life cycle of their clothing through proper 
 care techniques\, mending and alteration skills\, and creative up-cycling 
 workshops.\nThis Session: Conscious Consumption\nFashion industry impacts 
 & ethics\nReflection prompts & conversation about consumption habits\nShop
 ping literacy workshop with tips for spotting greenwashing & conscious sho
 pping\nJune 10th: Closing the Loop\nThe 7 R’s of circular fashion\nIdeas
  & practices for extending clothing lifespan keeping them in the loop\nEnd
  of life practices for textile waste\nJune 17th: Clothing & Caretaking\nMi
 ni hand sewing tutorials\nCreative brainstorming for participants' up-cycl
 ing piece\nJune 24th: Collaborative Mending & Upcycling\nParticipants will
  bring a piece of clothing that needs mending or upcycling & we will work 
 on them by hand together\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a049e6bc6a1dc3d00d379c0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
