BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fashion for the Planet: Closing the Loop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T200000
UID:6a04a0f9dcc3559e3b3bfea8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:With the rise of fast fashion brands and social media fueled c
 onsumption habits\, the fashion industry ranks as the 3rd most environment
 ally damaging industry. Everyone participates in this in some way\, so it 
 is important that people are given the information and tools to consume cl
 othing responsibly. This 4 session program will work towards providing sus
 tainable fashion literacy to participants by teaching them the environment
 al impacts of the fashion industry\, tips for conscious consumption\, and 
 practical tools to extend the life cycle of their clothing through proper 
 care techniques\, mending and alteration skills\, and creative up-cycling 
 workshops.\nThis Session\n: Closing the Loop\nThe 7 R’s of circular fash
 ion\nIdea & practices for extending clothing lifespan keeping them in the 
 loop\nEnd of life practices for textile waste\nJune 17th: Clothing & Caret
 aking\nMini hand sewing tutorials\nCreative brainstorming for participant
 ’s up-cycling piece\nJune 24th: Collaborative Mending & Upcycling\nParti
 cipants will bring a piece of clothing that needs mending or upcycling & w
 e will work on them by hand together\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04a0f9dcc3559e3b3bfea8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweetgrass Medicine Mist: An Infusion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T150000
UID:69de8a49b6c4ac1fedcc546e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn about the significa
 nce of sweetgrass from Indigenous perspective. Participants will also make
  a sweetgrass infusion that will later be strained and bottled to become a
  mist. All supplies are provided.\nDrop-in\, no registration required. Pro
 gram will be capped at the first 15 participants. Tickets will be handed o
 ut 30 minutes prior to start time.\nTanya Gluvakov is a mixed Mohawk woman
  from Toronto with family and "roots" from Six Nations of the Grand River 
 in Oshweken\, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven\, Tanya is a herbali
 st\, a mom\, a teacher\, and auntie\, who teaches several workshops about 
 medicines from the land and how connecting with them helps us find our way
 . She also leads several projects that bring the resurgence of medicines a
 nd accessibility to urban communities.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de8a49b6c4ac1fedcc546e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
