BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T180000
UID:69fcdb28f6bd012f00666189@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more?\nDrop in for the information session on Tue
 sday\, August 4\, 2026 at 3 pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Tuesday\,\no
 nce a week for 8 weeks\, August 11-September 29\, 2026 from 3 - 6 pm\n. Re
 gistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be
  provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ing
 redient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in colla
 boration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis
  Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information
  collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd floor at the end of the hallway.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcdb28f6bd012f00666189
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T153000
UID:69b1951a4dacf581ff812989@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning Python? Let's take a free online course
  together in a welcoming space!\nPython is a computer programming language
  used by startups and tech giants alike\, including Google\, Facebook\, Ne
 tflix and more.\nIn this 8-week learning circle\, we will work through ded
 icated course content together. The Python Essentials 1 course from the Op
 enEDG Python Institute teaches in-demand computer programming skills\, inc
 luding how to design\, develop\, and improve computer programs using the P
 ython programming language.\nWe will meet online every Tuesday afternoon\,
 \nMay 5 - June 23\n\, 2-3:30 PM\n.\nParticipants are expected to commit to
  the duration of the course and attend all learning circle sessions.\nLear
 ners who complete the course will be able to:\nEarn a digital badge\nDownl
 oad a certificate of completion\nReceive a 20% discount for the PCEP certi
 fication exam
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1951a4dacf581ff812989
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
