BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T200000
UID:697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e26f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the\ninformation session\non\nF
 riday\, April 24\, 2026.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a we
 ek for 8 weeks\, May 1 - June 19\, 2026\, 5:00-8:00pm\n. Registration clo
 ses after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSn
 acks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists 
 will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\
 nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is sol
 ely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected thr
 ough the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd floor\, end of hallway
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e26f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prompting with Generative AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T153000
UID:69dd0ec38ddc1caf5f1c9b8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn more about Generative AI through 
 hands-on activities? This program will teach you what makes an effective 
 prompt\, experiment with text and image generation\, and discover practica
 l ways to use AI tools for everyday and creative tasks. The session will a
 lso discuss best practices\, data privacy\, and ethical considerations to 
 help you use AI confidently and responsibly.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd0ec38ddc1caf5f1c9b8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
