DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T194500
UID:69e637d8f29b90618efee3ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The National Film Board revisits two documentaries from the su
 mmer of 1967\, one of teens travelling around and the other on the clash o
 ver the future of the hippie haven of Yorkville. Using original footage f
 rom 1967 and interviews years later with the documentary subjects. Just as
  the village of Yorkville has changed over time \, how much have the view
 s of the participants? To be preceded by a short visual presentation on th
 e history of Yorkville. There will be time for questions and comments at 
 the end. No registrations necessary.
