BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butterflies On The Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing Scree
 ning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of\nButterf
 lies on the Brink\n: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\n\, a gripping doc
 umentary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of
  extinction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes long\, followed by a Q&
 A panel with Miles Finlayson\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink\, 
 and special guest\nAdrienne Brewster\n\, Executive Director of Cambridge 
 Butterfly Conservatory.\nPresented by the\nDavid Suzuki Foundation (DSF)\n
 \, a Canadian environmental non-profit organization with a mission to prot
 ect nature’s diversity and the wellbeing of all life\, now and for the f
 uture.\nFree. Registration required. Doors open at 6:15 pm. At 6:30 pm\, s
 eating becomes first-come\, first-served until capacity is reached.\nThis 
 program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported b
 y Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nQuestions? Please
  contact North York Central Library - Business\, Science & Technology Depa
 rtment.\nThis program is also offered on\nThursday\, June 18\, 2026\, 6:3
 0 pm –8:00 pm\nat\nPalmerston Branch\n.\nYou can also find more\nDSF pro
 grams at TPL\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public L
 ibraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will on
 ly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
