BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Lillian Campbell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T235959
UID:69e7f7f1deee9abd8ee888d3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of May\, works by artist Lillian Campbell
  are on display at Agincourt Branch.\nLillian was born in Alberta and mov
 ed to Toronto in 2020. She has been painting nature since the age of 15\,
  when she used her brother‘s model paints and layers of old newspaper.\
 nFor Lillian's current art exhibit at the library\, she says: "I love nat
 ure and wish to share the world as I see it\, for everyone’s enjoyment."
 \nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Publ
 ic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locat
 ions across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural i
 nterests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed du
 ring\nAgincourt\nbranch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit:
  Lillian Campbell\; acrylic\; "Spring Flood"
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Hallway towards children's department
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e7f7f1deee9abd8ee888d3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
