DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T130000
UID:69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca85b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nThu
 rsday\, July 23\, 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\
 ,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, July 30-September 17\, 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Regi
 stration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be p
 rovided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingre
 dient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collabo
 ration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis C
 entre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information c
 ollected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca85b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T193000
UID:69ac44ff1e64afd01e606da2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Yorkville branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variet
 y of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the n
 atural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differe
 nt species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n
 The tour will start and end inside the Yorkville branch and will be guide
 d by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpav
 ed surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this
  outdoor program (sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program tak
 es place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, registr
 ants will be notified of an alternative date.\nChildren under 12 must be a
 ccompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Frag
 ile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Librar
 y\, South Chapter.​\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Meet in centre of library.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ac44ff1e64afd01e606da2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
