BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Recipe Club:  Food for Thought
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T193000
UID:6941dba7b5ff47300056f5e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy recipes and learning about food. Novice or chef e
 xtraordinaire\, drop in for an evening of culinary adventure.  Each month 
 we will delve into a different topic with lively and friendly  conversatio
 n. There will also be a selection of cookbooks to peruse and enjoy.  Last 
 year's book club created a 50-page recipe book to take home and enjoy.\nDr
 op In. No Registration Required.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6941dba7b5ff47300056f5e5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The True Crime Club at Taylor Memorial
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T200000
UID:6941dc7dfd55fb29005828f3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This club is for those who enjoy discussing  true crimes from 
 next door to around the world.  Each month we review a case and then we de
 cide which cases we want to look into next month   We investigate the case
 s on our own using a variety of true crime databases\, podcasts\, books et
 c.   We  then meet to discuss the theories and ideas  around the crime wit
 h one another. We are a passionate group and always discuss cases in a res
 pectful manner.  Come and join us on the second Tuesday of the month   for
  an intimate evening of  True Crime.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6941dc7dfd55fb29005828f3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
