BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T190000
UID:6a1752d6c7d3cd58005c239e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Em
 ergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with
  the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential
  hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to 
 assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks d
 uring emergencies\nFree program.\nRegistration required! For more informa
 tion\, please contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Rexdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1752d6c7d3cd58005c239e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T150000
UID:69459404293fe254002a353a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you love reading and talking about books?  Join us for an i
 nformal\, relaxed\, and casual meeting to discuss various books throughout
  the year.  The book club will meet monthly on the following dates:\nJanua
 ry 21:           Foster by Claire Keegan\nFebruary 18:\nThe Strange Eventf
 ul History by Claire Messud\nMarch 18:             The Ride of Her Life by
  Elizabeth Letts\nApril 15:                The Speckled Beauty by Rick Bra
 gg\nMay 20:                 The Librarianist by Patrick Dewitt\nJune 17: 
  Oh William! by Elizabeth Strout\nJuly 15: The Bookish Life of Nina Hill b
 y Abbi Waxman\nAugust 19: Cold Mountain by Charles Frazier\nSeptember 16: 
 Hotel on the Corner of Bitter and Sweet by Jamie Ford\nOctober 21: In the
  Upper Country by Kai Thomas\nNovember 18: Julie Chan is Dead by Liann Zhe
 ng\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69459404293fe254002a353a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
