BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grown-ups Reading Children's Literature Book Club: Heidi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T160000
UID:6996131a5506be0745fe2845@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the monthly meeting of Osborne Collection's Book C
 lub. In June we will be discussing\nHeidi\nby Johanna Spyri.\nGrown-ups Re
 ading Children's Literature Book Club is for adult readers who enjoy child
 ren's books. Revisit favourite stories of your childhood or read more or l
 ess known notable books for young readers for the first time.\nWe meet on
 ce a month on the first or second Saturday (2.30-4PM)\nAugust 8: Because 
 of Winn-Dixie by Kate DiCamillo\nSeptember 12: Island of the Blue Dolphins
  by Scott O’Dell\nOctober 3: A Series of Unfortunate Events: The Bad Beg
 inning by Lemony Snicket\nNovember 14: Borrowers by Mary Norton\nDecember 
 12: The BFG by Roald Dahl\nJanuary 9 (2027): Number the Stars by Lois Lowr
 y\nRegistration not required.\nHeidi
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Osborne Collection is located on the 4th floor
  of Lillian H. Smith library.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6996131a5506be0745fe2845
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T190000
UID:696a99674a9fd98b7f780516@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively and fun discussion about the selected boo
 k of the month.\nThis book club has relocated to Main Street Branch during
  Dawes Road Branch's closure. New club members are welcome. Each month's s
 election will be available after the previous month's meeting.\nMay 11 :\n
 All the Light We Cannot See\nby Anthony Doerr\nJune 8 :\nDucks\nby Kate Be
 aton\nJuly 13 :\nThe Mistress of Nothing\nby Kate Pullinger\nAugust 10 :\n
 The Museum of Extraordinary Things\nby Alice Hoffman\nRegistration is requ
 ired. Please register in-person or by calling 416-393-7700.
LOCATION:Main Street\, Basement Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696a99674a9fd98b7f780516
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
