BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Travel Talk: Algeria
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T113000
UID:6999ef41b48451fc3c042ff2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Algeria\, a former French colony\, is the largest country in A
 frica. Experienced tour organizer and presenter David Crichton presents hi
 s trip to cities including Algiers the capital\, Constantine\, Oran and Gh
 ardaia\, a province in desert areas.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6999ef41b48451fc3c042ff2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CONCERT: Shannon Butcher Duo - A Canadian Songbook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T190000
UID:69cbc4b31e64afd01e65d6ab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed jazz singer/songwriter Shannon Butcher  celebrates 
 the music of the true north\, strong and free!\nExpect to hear Shannon's s
 ignature style adding a jazz twist to iconic Canadian pop and folk songs\,
  alongside some hidden Canadian jazz gems. Come along with Shannon on a so
 nic tour of Toronto\, from the music of the Palais Royale big band hall to
  the folk coffee houses of Yorkville.\nNo advance registration nor free ti
 ckets required.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cbc4b31e64afd01e65d6ab
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
