BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T150000
UID:69971db881b67dfe32a75f16@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the second Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostl
 y contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an evening session to discuss the s
 ame book on the third Wednesday of each month at 7:00 p.m.  You are welc
 ome at either or both!\nMay 13\, 2026:\nSea of Tranquility\nby Emily St. J
 ohn Mandel [\nNote:\nthis is a change.]\nJune 10\, 2026:\nPrairie Edge\nby
  Conor Kerr\nJuly 8\, 2026:\nLiberation Day\nby George Saunders\nNote:\nno
  August meeting\nSeptember 9\, 2026:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober
  14\, 2026:\nMaybe You Should Talk to Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 
 11\, 2026:\nStone Yard Devotional\nby Charlotte Wood\nDecember 9\, 2026:\n
 Perfection\nby Vincenzo Latronico
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69971db881b67dfe32a75f16
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Board Game Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T200000
UID:698387dab0595799c09ac124@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adult Board Game Social – Tabletop Gaming Mondays\nJoin us m
 onthly at the Malvern Library for Adult Board Game Social\, a relaxed even
 ing of tabletop games and good company.\nHave a favourite board game? Feel
  free to bring it along and share it with others. Shorter and easy-to-lear
 n games work best\, but there is always room to explore something new toge
 ther.\nThe library will also provide a selection of board games for casual
  play. No experience needed. This is a welcoming\, low-pressure space to l
 earn\, play\, and connect with others.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698387dab0595799c09ac124
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
