SUMMARY:Journalism Series with David Silverberg: What do editors want from
  freelance journalists? (panel discussion)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
UID:69c81fe8b48451fc3c0bd8f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This panel discussion is presented by the North York Central 
 Library's 2026 Writer in Residence David Silverberg\, whose focus is on Jo
 urnalism.\nLearn from editors who have witnessed it all. Joining David on 
 a panel discussion to share their insight on ideas they’d like to see fr
 om freelance journalists\, Toronto-based editors Navneet Alang (opinions 
 editor\, The Toronto Star)\, Judith Pereira (arts editor\, The Globe & Mai
 l)\, and Malcolm Johnston (editor-in-chief\, Toronto Life) will reveal t
 heir favourite pitches and discuss the types of articles they publish. The
  panel will also discuss pay rates\, developing relationships with editors
  and their top Do’s and Don’ts.\nThis discussion will be followed by Q
 &A\nLearn more about TPL's\nWriter in Residence\nprogram\, including upcom
 ing programs and one-on-one consultation sessions.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
