BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Lama Al Ghatrif
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T235959
UID:6a0506a0caf93436005bc949@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Lama Al Ghatrif
  are on display at Agincourt Branch.\nRaised between Syria and the UAE\, L
 ama is an internationally trained architect who moved to Canada in 2019. H
 er creative journey is rooted in a lifelong passion for drawing that preda
 tes her architectural career. Since graduating in 2010\, Lama has balance
 d the technical discipline of design with a dedicated fine arts practice\,
  specializing in realistic charcoal portraiture and expressive mixed-media
 . Her work explores the intersection of structural precision and emotive s
 torytelling—a global perspective shaped by a life of transition across b
 orders and disciplines.\n"\nArchitecture provides the framework for our li
 ves\, but drawing captures the essence of our living."\nThis exhibit is pa
 rt of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides 
 space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city
 . These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city
  and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nAgincourt\nbra
 nch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Lama Al Ghatrif\; c
 harcoal and golden leaf on paper\; "Finding the Light"
LOCATION:Agincourt\, First floor hallway towards the Children's Department
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0506a0caf93436005bc949
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Animals to Abstract Artwork by Jackie Lewis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T235959
UID:69ed072bc1cf6f9a7587c43f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of May\, the works of artist Jackie Lewis
  are on display at Leaside branch in an exhibit titled\nAnimals to Abstrac
 t Artwork\n.\nJackie was always the class artist in school and won three
  Lions Club awards for their art. They studied art with James Spencer who 
 has two of his mountain paintings in the National Gallery in Ottawa. They
  have made art work for thirty years.\n"I am very in-tune with my painting
 s channeling love and light to assist both myself and the viewer."\nThis e
 xhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library prov
 ides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the
  city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the
  city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nLeaside B
 ranch\nopen hours. Please check the Leaside Branch page before your visit.
 \nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Jackie Lewis\; Title of Pi
 ece: Young Tiger\; Medium: Acrylic\; Size/Dimensions: up to 20 x 25 cm
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ed072bc1cf6f9a7587c43f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T163000
UID:69ee56c31e64afd01e6bd84d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When we write with others\, we discover ourselves\n.\nWriters 
 Collective of Canada (WCC) workshops offer a brave creative space where al
 l are welcomed to write and explore their story in a space free of critiqu
 e.\nThe workshops are led by trained volunteer facilitators who also act a
 s participants. The group writes in response to prompts\, is invited to sh
 are their first draft writing\, and offers affirming feedback to one anoth
 er.\nWhile the focus is on the process of writing rather than a finished p
 roduct\, the stories that emerge in WCC workshops are magnificent. In shar
 ing and listening to one another's stories\, participants find connection 
 with self and others.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. All 
 materials are provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ee56c31e64afd01e6bd84d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
