BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Games Week: Secrets of MUDs and MUSHes from a Werewolf Eld
 er
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
UID:6a0dfd060c0f2c4503fac3e7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come learn about the history of MUDs and MUSHes from a longtim
 e RetroMUX community Storyteller! Find out how the very first online rolep
 laying games persist after more than 45 years\, plus\, come play (bring a 
 laptop\, tablet\, or phone!) on a noob-friendly MUSH set in cyberpunk Toro
 nto specially designed for TGW.\nFree\, just show up! More information vi
 a link at\nTorontoGamesWeek.com/schedule
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dfd060c0f2c4503fac3e7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de North York Central Library
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
UID:6a0dfd67278f7c2f008e700f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Aimez-vous lire en français? Avez-vous envie de participer à
  des discussions autour des livres dans une ambiance conviviale et déten
 due?\nRejoignez notre club de lecture en français! Venez échanger vos po
 ints de vue\, analyser ce qui vous a marqué avec le regard d'autres lecte
 urs\, et faire de belles découvertes littéraires.\nOn se réunit le jeud
 i 25 juin pour découvrir\n« L'étoile russe » d'Anne-Marie Revol\n. Le 
 livre sera disponible en prêt à la Bibliothèque de North York Central\n
 \, au 3ième étage\, Département de langues\, littérature et beaux arts
  à partir du 20 mai.\nSi vous voulez en savoir plus sur nos clubs de lec
 tures\, veuillez nous envoyer un courriel à\nprogrammesenfrancais@tpl.ca\
 nVeuillez noter que ce programme s’adresse aux personnes francophones ai
 nsi qu’à celles ayant un niveau avancé en français. Il est nécessair
 e de pouvoir lire\, discuter et critiquer un livre avec une aisance de com
 munication en français.\nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre français mais
  que vous avez plutôt un niveau débutant ou intermédiaire\, nous vous e
 ncourageons à découvrir nos cercles de conversation.\nLe sous-titrage en
  direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les se
 rvices d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibl
 es sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à
  l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dfd67278f7c2f008e700f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Games Week: For the Fans! Fan Merch Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T200000
UID:6a0dfd9646d5f64f7dcc579e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Buying physical merch for your fandom? In this economy?? Fret 
 not because this beginner-friendly workshop will provide the supplies and 
 guidance for creating your very own fan merch! Come make ribbon badges\, p
 ins\, zines\, and more while learning about fan merch etiquette and histor
 y.\nFree! Registration required. More information via link at\nTorontoGa
 mesWeek.com/schedule
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dfd9646d5f64f7dcc579e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sounds That Shape Play: A Toronto Game Audio Roundtable
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T200000
UID:6a0dfd9fa99bdd027d425858@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Toronto Game Audio Collective (TGAC)\, this inte
 ractive roundtable session will bring together game audio creatives from a
 cross the GTA to connect to\, learn from\, and inspire one another. At thi
 s roundtable\, we will explore how composers and audio artists can lead a 
 game’s creative direction through sound.\nThis session is open to all pr
 ofessional\, aspiring and enthusiasts of video game audio!\nFree. Registra
 tion required. More information via link at\nTorontoGamesWeek.com/schedule
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, In program room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dfd9fa99bdd027d425858
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open World Map: Digital Sovereignty for Game Creators
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
UID:6a0dfe10e13d3b4603b4e5cb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enshittified platforms and proprietary tools are not only maki
 ng the world worse\, but they make it harder for game creators to connect 
 with an audience. But as tech-savvy systems thinkers\, game creators are u
 niquely positioned to push back in a number of ways.\nJoin us for an inspi
 ring day of discussion\, demos\, and workshops featuring: open source game
  dev tool alternatives from Matt Hammill (Lovers in a Dangerous Spacetime)
 \, Mastodon tips and tricks from Rob Gehl (Move Slowly and Build Bridges f
 rom Oxford Press)\, playing with open protocols with Christine Lemmer-Webb
 er and David Thompson (ActivityPub and Spritely Foundation)\, and liberati
 ng D&D data with Cousin Vagabond!\nFree. Registration required. More info
 rmation via link at\nTorontoGamesWeek.com/schedule
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, In Program Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dfe10e13d3b4603b4e5cb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BIKE MONTH: Learn to Maintain Your Bike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
UID:6a0e0412fab4ff0f649a7353@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get yourself (and your tires) pumped up for bike month with th
 e ABCs of bike maintenance. Led by branch staff\, topics covered include b
 rake & gear adjustments\, tires & tubes and the ABC quick check. This work
 shop will be taking place outdoors (weather permitting)\; participants are
  welcome to bring their own bicycles.  If the program moves indoors due 
 to poor conditions\, bikes will need to be left outside the branch (bike p
 osts are available for locking bikes).\nRegistration Required\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Annette Street
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0e0412fab4ff0f649a7353
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
