BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:High Park Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T200000
UID:6a15c48043b41b3d00692adf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and join us on the second Wednesday of every month to dis
 cuss a variety of books. Everyone is welcome!\nJanuary 14:\nWhat I Mean t
 o Say\n: Remaking Conversation in Our Time by Ian Williams\nFebruary 11:\n
 Fahrenheit 451\nby Ray Bradbury\nMarch 11:\nThe Remains of the Day\nby Kaz
 uo Ishiguro\nApril 8:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nMay 13:\nThe Empusium\
 n: A Health Resort Horror Story by Olga Tokarczuk\nJune 10:\nTruth Telling
 \nSeven Conversations About Indigenous Life in Canada by Michelle Good\nJu
 ly 8:\nThree Days in June\nby Anne Tyler\nAugust 12:\nThe Woman in the Lib
 rary\nby Sulari Gentill
LOCATION:High Park\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a15c48043b41b3d00692adf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
