BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fact or Fiction: Identifying and Combatting Misinformation and Di
 sinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T153000
UID:6a162de78ea300e26318bd1c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds of all ages who want to arm th
 emselves with the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of onlin
 e information responsibly and safely.\nNote: This is a User Education cla
 ss\, on laptops. Laptops will be provided for use during this class.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a162de78ea300e26318bd1c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Game Night: Murder Mystery!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T200000
UID:6a04e303c7d3cd580059058e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Step into a night of intrigue\, laughter\, and just a little b
 it of deception. Join us for a\nmurder mystery game\nwhere everyone has a 
 role to play—and a secret to hide. Expect an evening filled with twists\
 , clues\, and questionable alibis as you work together (or against each ot
 her) to uncover the culprit. With a light script to guide you\, no acting
  skills are required… just a willingness to have fun and embrace the une
 xpected. Costumes are welcome but not required -- your wit is your best ac
 cessory.\nGame Synopsis:\nYou’re invited to Heathcliff Manor\, where Lor
 d Heathcliff is hosting a dinner party in honour of his new bride. All the
  usual suspects are here - the cook\, the professor\, the butler - as well
  as some unusual ones. But before anyone can toast his happiness\, Lord He
 athcliff is killed with the candlestick in the pool room. You and the othe
 r guests must uncover clues related to motive and method to catch the kil
 ler before the night ends.\nWhat to expect:\n• A fun\, guided murder my
 stery game\n• Light role-playing with provided scripts\n• A relaxed\, 
 social atmosphere\n• Plenty of laughs and surprises\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04e303c7d3cd580059058e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
