BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NFB Film Screening: Wilfred Buck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T150000
UID:6a18447cf56bd86e00b2b71d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a\nNational Film Board of Canada\nfilm screening t
 his National Indigenous History Month\, and learn more about Cree Elder an
 d astronomer\,\nWilfred Buck\n!\nHis name is He Has Dreamt a Dream and Kee
 ps It\, but most know him as Wilfred Buck\, the Star Man. In his own words
 \, he is “of the fresh-out-of-the-bush\, partly civilized\, colonized\, 
 displaced people.” A charismatic Cree Elder with a sly wit\, Wilfred is 
 known for collecting the knowledge of Cree astronomy and sharing it across
  generations. His teachings have taken him from lecture halls to sweat lod
 ges\, transcending the boundaries of Western science. Intimate yet expansi
 ve\, Wilfred Buck is a time-travelling road trip through a harrowing histo
 ry of displacement and racism\, from growing up in 1960s Northern Manitoba
  to Wilfred’s reconnection with the cosmological wisdom of his people. C
 ombining cinematic re-enactments\, archival footage and beautiful celestia
 l imagery with Buck’s unmistakable laugh\, director Lisa Jackson takes u
 s on a journey to the space beyond\, and to the spaces between us all.\nDo
 cumentary is rated PG\, run-time approximately 96 minutes.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Auditorium (FCCR)\, first floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a18447cf56bd86e00b2b71d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T113000
UID:6a1881c40c0f2c4503fb8ffc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (F1)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1881c40c0f2c4503fb8ffc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T150000
UID:6a18abbc46d5f64f7dcd3698@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nJune 3:\nE.T. The
  Extra-Terrestrial\nJune 10:\nMadagascar 2\nJune 17:\nAbout a Boy\nJune 24
 :\nIndiana Jones and the Raiders of the Lost Ark\nJuly 8:\nAlmost Famous\
 nJuly 15: Starman (1984)\nJuly 22:\nA Star is Born\n(2018)\nJuly 29:\nBrid
 get Jones Diary\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshmen
 ts are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available 
 at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Ce
 ntre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a18abbc46d5f64f7dcd3698
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
